  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Senior Design Project - Sensor Skin",
    "description": "The Sensor Skin is a small consumer device used afford \"smart\" capabilities to appliances without this ability.  A practical example may be a dryer which, with the Sensor Skin attached, will automatically send an alert to the user when a laundry cycle has completed.\n\nAn array of sensors is employed to measure the operational behavior of the appliance and the characteristics of its surroundings.  Signal processing algorithms are applied to the data collected and the definition of a particular state can be extracted.  Using the example of the dryer, a \"normal dry\" state may be detected by the presence of known dominant vibration signatures and a measured case temperature within the known range.  \n\nA web interface was also created to communicate with the device.  In the event that the user would like to move the Sensor Skin to a new target, selecting the new appliance from the interface initiates a calibration routine which reconfigures the device, enabling only the necessary sensors and optimizing the power reduction protocol for the new application.  ",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Feb 2013 - Aug 2013"
